# avmeasure self-test session -- NOT for human use, NOT therapeutic.
# Exists only so the test suite has a session that exercises every measurement:
# a sync marker, two light channels, a binaural pair, an isochronic pulse, an
# audio-only step and a light-only step (so a fault can be aimed at exactly one
# domain).
#
# LED columns  : time(ms) freq duty bright R G B mask
# Audio columns: A time(ms) freq pan vol mod ch freqR wave

# --- sync marker: 600 ms of 50 Hz full-brightness light + a 3 kHz tone ---
#     See README "sync marker recipe". 50 Hz raises the flicker ISR tick to its
#     10 kHz ceiling for the whole session, which makes the later 10/20 Hz
#     rates land exactly on tick boundaries -- deliberate, so this session
#     tests the comparator rather than the quantization model (which has its
#     own unit test against hand-computed values).
0       50 50 100 255 255 255 3
A 0     3000 0 70 0 15
600     0 50 0 0 0 0 3
A 600   3000 0 0 0 15

# --- body: ch1 + ch2 at 10 Hz / 50% / 60%; binaural 240|246 (6 Hz beat),
#     gated at 7 Hz ---
1000    10 50 60 255 255 255 1
1000    10 50 60 255 255 255 2
A 1000  240 0 50 7 1 246 0

# --- AUDIO-ONLY step at 30 s: volume 50 -> 25. No light entry shares this
#     timestamp, so a 'late' fault here lands purely on the audio path. ---
A 30000 240 0 25 7 1 246 0

# --- LIGHT-ONLY step at 60 s: ch1 10 Hz -> 20 Hz. No audio entry shares this
#     timestamp, so a 'drop' fault here lands purely on the light path. ---
60000   20 50 60 255 255 255 1

# --- end: brightness 0 on the last entry. config_parser.c:2104-2111 stops all
#     flicker in the same dispatch as the last batch, so a last entry that
#     still asks for light would be cancelled before it ever emits an edge --
#     which the linter flags as LEDC_LAST_ENTRY_CANCELLED. Ending at 0 makes
#     the intent explicit, and is what every shipped session does. ---
90000   20 50 0 255 255 255 1
90000   10 50 0 255 255 255 2
A 90000 240 0 0 7 1 246 0
